    "submission": "submission-f2-scope.json",
    "summary": "Turn 62 filed the F2 scope clarification that the open bookkeeping issue needed, using the accepted C3 claim as its basis.\n\nWhy an F2. The one visible administrative debt is that the superseded C1 artifact asserted an applied-state predicate outside C1's accepted scope. Earlier attempts to resolve it were each refused for a specific reason (resolution on another artifact, an ordinary repair that must preserve the oracle, an encoding correction that needs an oracle or observation challenge), so the mechanism that remains is an F2 semantic revision of the C1 claim itself.\n\nWhat the F2 changes. The patch replaces C1-recovery-adopts-committed-vector with the same id, obligation, sources, kind and pending fields, adding one clause to the scope description and one excluded item: the obligation ends at adopting the reported committed vector, and applied-state agreement for a committed instance is claim C3-applied-effect-follows-committed-vector's proposition rather than C1's. The declared judgment change is the scope field with its old and new JSON, the old/new judgments contrast the ambiguity with the explicit boundary, the new basis is C3's own reviewed check, and the grounding cites the executor and state-application sources that establish where the applied effect lives, bound to the existing C3 binding.\n\nThe submission went through four validator rules, each recorded: the persisted claim carries fields the draft schema forbids (stripped to the claim-draft shape), evidence ids must be checks or materials (the artifact id was dropped in favour of C3's experiment check and two material sources), replacing an object requires its expected version (the accepted C1 claim is version 1), and the grounding must share a source with the evidence. With those satisfied the preflight passes.\n\nEffect. If accepted, the C1 claim itself states the boundary that the challenged artifact blurred, so the open scope issue has an answer on the claim's own terms without touching any artifact, requirement, condition, binding or observation; the ten settled findings and the two paused candidates are unaffected, and no requirement or premise was weakened."
